From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jiangcuo <itsupport@lierfang.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libperf cpumap: fix -Werror=alloc-size-larger-than with GCC 13

GCC 13 cannot prove that the int sum/max of the two map sizes is
non-negative, so it assumes the malloc() size may wrap to a huge
size_t value and fails the build on loong64:

  cpumap.c: In function 'perf_cpu_map__merge':
  error: argument 1 range [18446744065119617024, 18446744073709551612]
  exceeds maximum object size 9223372036854775807
  [-Werror=alloc-size-larger-than=]

Bail out early when the length is not positive. Both maps are non-NULL
and non-empty at this point, so this does not change behaviour.

---
 tools/lib/perf/cpumap.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/tools/lib/perf/cpumap.c
+++ b/tools/lib/perf/cpumap.c
@@ -419,6 +419,8 @@
 	}
 
 	tmp_len = __perf_cpu_map__nr(orig) + __perf_cpu_map__nr(other);
+	if (tmp_len <= 0)
+		return NULL;
 	tmp_cpus = malloc(tmp_len * sizeof(struct perf_cpu));
 	if (!tmp_cpus)
 		return NULL;
@@ -461,6 +463,8 @@
 		return perf_cpu_map__get(other);
 
 	tmp_len = max(__perf_cpu_map__nr(orig), __perf_cpu_map__nr(other));
+	if (tmp_len <= 0)
+		return NULL;
 	tmp_cpus = malloc(tmp_len * sizeof(struct perf_cpu));
 	if (!tmp_cpus)
 		return NULL;
-- 
2.39.5
